      "releaseNotes": "1.4.4\n“The one that fixes slowdowns over time”\n\nLove Greyline? Stop by my Ko-Fi! https://ko-fi.com/kb0rb \n\n**NOTE** - The WRL logging API is a work in progress, and I will continue to improve the app as their API evolves! What we have here now takes full advantage of what the service currently supports. Stay tuned for more features!\n\nBe sure to check the release notes for prior versions to see what's new! I update the app regularly in response to feedback like yours. Read them at https://greylineft8.com/changelog.html\n\nRemember that Greyline now has a comprehensive user manual at https://greylineft8.com/userguide.html - you’ll also find a button in the Settings view to take you there\n\nShoutouts:\nK7DFS: Reporting slowdown issues in the waterfall and filter view\nON4LDZ: Reporting delayed transmissions and waterfall latency\n\nFeatures:\n- WRL logging now supports the “myActivities” field, which allows individual contacts to be marked with a POTA reference ID. Note that if you have entered an invalid POTA reference ID, it will be dropped when the contact is uploaded to WRL, due to how their API is structured.\n\nFixes\n- Long running sessions could drift far off the correct mode timing, due to a math error in the sampling view.\n- The “Only my exchanges and CQ” filter could sometimes cause the band activity view to freeze up\n- Added a new “Timing Health” section to the in-app diagnostics\n\nThat’s it, that’s all, folks! Thanks for bringing me on your activations - now get out there and POTA on. 73!",
